# Per-Dockerfile ignore for `docker build -f mayhem/Dockerfile .`. BuildKit gives this
# file precedence over the repo-root .dockerignore, whose `.git/` exclusion would break
# our build: the mayhem.yml CI checkout is fetch-depth 0 and the Dockerfile COPYs .git
# into /mayhem (the grader / PATCH tier need the full `mayhem` branch history).
#
# So we KEEP .git and the whole source tree (near-primitives' path-dep chain spans many
# core/ + utils/ crates) and only drop build artifacts.
**/target
mayhem/fuzz/target
mayhem/kat/target
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
